"position":"1787579506768522001-b0444895-3b15-4be3-b969-3848bb6c64cc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787017356659244001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"5cf2eb05-1489-482b-9dea-3eb5ed8e2062","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"1d22-40ba-8e2b-4f67"},{"link_uuid":"72249f3b-00bc-4244-9aba-fe8c077ab26c","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"b612-1edb-efa9-4c61"},{"link_uuid":"41a0d69f-e728-4ce1-94c9-ef8e91b009ca","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f066-103b-d823-49ea"},{"link_uuid":"d053c730-c39a-400d-a873-6773ce30789b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1174-72f3-8714-42d1"},{"link_uuid":"019d332f-a612-4d74-897c-c1bd695bce3f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1b49-cce9-f0de-40e1"}],"description":"## Context\n\nMigrate eligible OpenAI providers to the pydantic-ai **Responses API** as a config cutover with a\npre-v1 deprecation of the Chat-Completions fallback. The blocking research ticket\n`ageless-ferny-ugandakob` (b612-1edb-efa9-4c61, CLOSED) produced the capability matrix and the\ncontract tests (`tests/unit/test_openai_responses_contract.py`, already landed and green for both\nprefixes). Its verdict, which this ticket implements verbatim:\n\n- **Only hosted OpenAI (matrix row 1)** — bare `openai:`/inferred `gpt-*`/`o1`/`o3`/`chatgpt`,\n  with NO custom endpoint — is Responses-ready under the pinned pydantic-ai 1.107.2.\n- **Every other row is Chat-Completions-only or UNKNOWN** and stays on `openai-chat:`:\n  custom `base_url` builder (row 2), per-candidate `endpoint` override (row 3), `gateway/openai`\n  (4), `deepseek`/`grok`/`moonshotai`/`heroku`/`cerebras` (5-7), `xai`/`groq` (8, UNKNOWN),\n  vendor-side `/v1/responses` (9, UNKNOWN/moot under the pin).\n- The migration's edit-set is the **four constraint sites** the matrix named.\n\nOperator decision (2026-08-19, recorded on this ticket): **config cutover APPROVED** with a\nper-provider fallback to `openai-chat:` that is **explicitly temporary** — it carries a\ndeprecation notice and is **scheduled for removal before v1**.\n\n## Design\n\n**Default flip (the cutover).** Hosted OpenAI now resolves to `openai-responses:` by default. A\ncustom OpenAI-compatible endpoint (top-level `base_url`, per-class slot `endpoint`, or\nper-candidate `endpoint`) keeps resolving to `openai-chat:` — matrix rows 2-3: rebar's\n`_build_openai` registers only under `openai`/`openai-chat`, an `openai-responses:` string never\nreaches it, and vendor `/v1/responses` support for custom servers is UNKNOWN, so flipping a\ncustom endpoint would silently ignore its `base_url`.\n\n**The fallback IS the explicit `openai-chat:` qualifier** (or `provider = \"openai-chat\"`), now a\nDEPRECATED compatibility surface. It is per-provider/per-slot because each model-class slot,\nfallback candidate, or `cfg.model` names its own qualifier. Writing it for **hosted** OpenAI emits\na once-per-run deprecation notice pointing to `openai-responses:`, registered in the central\n`rebar._deprecations` registry as `cfg:openai-chat` with `remove_in = \"v1.0.0\"` (the repo's\nsingle-sourced pre-v1 removal horizon `_deprecations._MAJOR`). Chat forced by a **custom\nendpoint** does NOT warn (it is a construction constraint, not a deprecated opt-in, and no\nResponses alternative exists for it).\n\nPortability: this is a pure config-resolution/provider change with no CI-provider dependency; the\ndeprecation horizon is a static repo constant, and all new tests run in-process against an\n`httpx.MockTransport` stub with no network or provider credentials.\n\n## Edit-set (RED->GREEN)\n\n1. `src/rebar/llm/config.py` — add `\"openai-responses\"` to `KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES` so\n   `split_provider_qualifier`/`infer_provider` treat `openai-responses:` as a qualifier.\n2. `src/rebar/llm/providers.py` — add `openai-responses` to the set\n   `_pydantic_ai_known_providers()` returns (a new `_EXTRA_KNOWN_PROVIDERS` frozenset for names\n   `infer_provider` special-cases but `known_model_names()` omits), so\n   `ProviderSession.is_resolvable(\"openai-responses\")` is True and the runner leaves it a lazy\n   string for pydantic-ai to build `OpenAIResponsesModel`. The rebar builder stays chat-only.\n3. `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py` — add `\"openai-responses\": _resolve_openai` to\n   `_PROFILE_RESOLVERS` so capability resolution no longer degrades (native_structured_output\n   parity with `openai-chat:`).\n4. `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py` — `_resolve_target` grows an `endpoint: str | None = None`\n   param; an `_openai_family_target(tail, requested, endpoint)` helper returns `openai-chat:` for\n   an explicit `openai-chat` request or when an endpoint is present, else `openai-responses:`\n   (keeps `_resolve_target` under the C901 ceiling). Thread `endpoint` from the callers that hold\n   it: `resolve_class`/`resolve_fallback_chain` (slot/target endpoint), `primary_endpoint_for`,\n   `fallback_targets_for`, `build_fallback_model` — so the identity-matching those functions do on\n   `_resolve_target` output stays consistent with what `resolve_class` produced.\n5. `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py` — `_pai_model`: explicit `openai-chat:` passes through;\n   bare `openai:` resolves to `openai-chat:` when `cfg.base_url` is set, else `openai-responses:`.\n6. `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` — after `resolved` and the effective `cfg.base_url` (incl. recovered\n   slot endpoint) are known, emit the `cfg:openai-chat` notice once when `resolved` is hosted\n   `openai-chat:` (starts with `openai-chat:` AND no `base_url`).\n7. `src/rebar/_deprecations.py` — register the `cfg:openai-chat` scheduled deprecation.\n8. Docs: `docs/config-reference.md` + `docs/llm-framework.md` — document the wire-semantic change,\n   how to exercise the `openai-chat:` fallback, its deprecation and the `v1.0.0` removal target.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Update the intended behavioural-diff assertions (now `openai-responses:` for hosted openai):\n  `tests/unit/test_provider_qualifier.py` (incl. the `_KNOWN_24`->`_KNOWN_25` drift set),\n  `tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py`, `tests/unit/test_model_classes.py`,\n  `tests/unit/test_llm_capabilities.py`.\n- New assertions: hosted `openai:`/`gpt-4o` -> `openai-responses:`; `openai:` + endpoint (top-level\n  and per-slot) stays `openai-chat:`; explicit `openai-chat:` stays chat; `is_resolvable` and\n  capabilities parity for `openai-responses:`; the deprecation notice fires once for hosted\n  `openai-chat:` and NOT for endpoint-forced chat.\n- Re-run the landed contract tests (already parameterized over both prefixes) as the wire-level\n  behavioural diff.\n- Gates: focused provider tests plus `make test`, `make lint`, `make typecheck` in this worktree.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Every provider the matrix marks Responses-ready (hosted OpenAI, row 1) resolves to\n      `openai-responses:` explicitly; every retained `openai-chat:` path (custom endpoints, rows\n      2-3; other vendors, rows 4-9) is justified by the cited matrix row.\n- [x] The contract tests are re-run against the migrated paths and the behavioural diff is\n      recorded (structured output, streaming, tool calls, retries, custom base URLs).\n- [x] A per-provider fallback to `openai-chat:` exists, is documented, emits a deprecation notice,\n      and has a named pre-v1 removal target (`v1.0.0`) recorded via the deprecation registry.\n- [x] Configuration/migration docs explain the observable wire-semantic changes and how to\n      exercise the fallback.\n- [x] Focused provider tests plus `make test`, `make lint`, `make typecheck` pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/config.py","reason":"add openai-responses to KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES so it is a recognized provider qualifier"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/providers.py","reason":"recognize openai-responses in _pydantic_ai_known_providers so is_resolvable is true; builder stays chat-only"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py","reason":"add openai-responses profile resolver so capability resolution does not degrade"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py","reason":"flip hosted openai default to openai-responses; keep custom endpoints on openai-chat via endpoint-aware _resolve_target"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py","reason":"_pai_model: bare openai -> openai-responses when no base_url, openai-chat when custom endpoint"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/runner.py","reason":"emit once-per-run openai-chat deprecation notice for hosted chat"},{"path":"src/rebar/_deprecations.py","reason":"register cfg:openai-chat scheduled deprecation with v1.0.0 removal"},{"path":"docs/config-reference.md","reason":"document wire-semantic cutover, fallback, deprecation and removal target"},{"path":"docs/llm-framework.md","reason":"document the openai-responses default and the openai-chat fallback"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_provider_qualifier.py","reason":"update intended resolution diffs and drift set to include openai-responses"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py","reason":"update _pai_model/_resolve_target expectations to openai-responses"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_model_classes.py","reason":"update resolve_class expectations; add endpoint-stays-chat cases"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_llm_capabilities.py","reason":"add openai-responses capability parity cases"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_openai_responses_migration.py","reason":"new tests: default flip, endpoint-forces-chat, deprecation notice emission"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","b612-1edb-efa9-4c61"],["relates_to","1174-72f3-8714-42d1"],["relates_to","1b49-cce9-f0de-40e1"],["relates_to","f066-103b-d823-49ea"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"9896dd34-5e2a-4941-a86e-a875f5f76823","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["pydantic-ai","provider","migration"],"ticket_id":"155c-218b-c128-4700","ticket_type":"story","title":"Migrate eligible OpenAI providers to the pydantic-ai Responses API (config cutover with pre-v1 deprecation)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["40016cca-1f84-4dff-9e52-15e167de3592","72249f3b-00bc-4244-9aba-fe8c077ab26c","8bc735d3-9e1d-4aae-b1e0-bc8c95956d3f","af7768fc-385a-400a-8eda-685cffb384b4","3668eb05-87fc-45af-9b51-cae143e15e42","89f8cb79-b367-4551-9b54-fc268bda3e2f","ce4f1f6c-1843-49fa-9b79-8e6fd4ce6625","41a0d69f-e728-4ce1-94c9-ef8e91b009ca","d053c730-c39a-400d-a873-6773ce30789b","019d332f-a612-4d74-897c-c1bd695bce3f","d7419c0c-60eb-4b30-a060-b06c02bf1072","9896dd34-5e2a-4941-a86e-a875f5f76823","b0444895-3b15-4be3-b969-3848bb6c64cc"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787584506919860001,"uuid":"9da1fc0c-694f-44ef-939c-559704447585"}